clients/ts/**/dist/
clients/ts/tessera.toml
# Everything `run_demo.sh` produces — bundles, caches, WALs, the deployments it generates, the
# measured presets and the dataset document naming what is actually being served. Facts about an
# invocation rather than about the repository, which is why the demo writes none of them into the
# source tree and why a second session can put them elsewhere with `TESSERA_DEMO_DIR`.
/tessera-demo/
# Where `publish-clusters.mjs` put the clusters it published into *this* server's WAL. Layers live
# in the WAL rather than the bundle, so the names in it mean nothing to another server — and the
# script is re-run per server anyway, a layer name never being reusable.
clients/ts/viewer/public/clusters.json
*.env.local
clients/ts/.vite.out
